## Files you write
{{if .Wants "app.json"}}- app.json: id, name, space ("{{.Space}}"), version 1, kit 2, agent {name, file: "agent.md", model: "{{.AgentModel}}"}, records, capabilities, triggers, commands, budget. Record ids = the plan's data ids. Field types: text longtext number money date datetime duration enum enums bool person people ref refs email phone url file files place. A field with `"ai": "<question>"` is an AI field.
  - Make the data useful: give every record type `label`, `plural`, `title` (the field that names it) and every field the plan lists, plus any obvious one it implies (a status or stage as `enum` with `values` in workflow order, a date, an owner as `person` with default "$me", money as `money`). Relations are `ref`/`refs` with `to`. Mark the name field `required`.
  - capabilities.records: "rw" for every record type. Declare `ai` or `connectors` only when the plan needs them. Set budget from: {{.Budget}}.{{if .Connectors}} Connected: {{join .Connectors ", "}}.{{else}} No accounts are connected, so declare no connectors.{{end}}
  - triggers and commands exist only for plan automations; each points at a run id.
{{end}}{{if .Wants "screens/"}}- screens/<id>.json: one per plan screen; file name = screen id. Root keys: screen, title, params, nav, body. A node is `{part, id, label, props, bind, on, when, children, slots}`. `nav` is the one SectionTabs, `props.items` = the titles of all plan screens in plan order. Every interactive node has a `label`. Props only from the catalog. Binds: `{"records":type,"query":q}` (a list), `{"record":"$params.id","type":type}` (one record), `{"run":id,"for":"$params.id"}`, `{"approvals":"open"}`. Actions in `on`: open, records.create, records.update, records.delete, runs.start, approve, agent.ask, ai.sort. Strings may hold {{"{{template}}"}} values; refs are $me $params.x $row $selection.<id>.ids|.id|.count $input.x.
  Build screens a person can work in, not placeholders:
  - A LIST screen (for a main record type): a Row with a Text title (size "title") and a primary Button "New <thing>" whose click is `{"records.create":{"type":T,"set":{field:"$input.field",...}},"ask":{field:fieldtype,...}}`, asking the required fields and up to five more (ask types: text longtext number money date enum bool email phone url). Under it a RecordList (id, label, bind with a `sort:` query, `columns` of 4 to 6 fields, `on.open` → `{"open":"<detail screen>","id":"$row.id"}`, `slots.empty` an Empty with a short text). When the type has a status/stage enum, add `views: ["List","Board by <field>"]`, `groupBy` and `meter` on that field. Where a number or money field exists, put a Chart (`chart` "metric", `agg` "sum" or "count") or a bar Chart by the enum above the list.
  - A DETAIL screen (params ["id"]): a RecordPage bound to `$params.id` with `fields` listing every field and `history` true; a Row of Buttons: "Edit <thing>" (records.update of `$params.id` with `ask` for the editable fields), the plan's run buttons (runs.start), and "Delete <thing>…" (kind destructive, records.delete with `confirm`, then open the list screen). Add RunTimeline / ApprovalCard only if the app has runs.
  - A SUMMARY screen when the plan names one (board, dashboard, overview): Charts and a RecordList, no forms.
  - Every screen opened by `open` must be a plan screen id. A record type with no list screen of its own gets its detail screen only if the plan lists it.
{{end}}{{if .Wants "runs/"}}- runs/<id>.yaml: one per plan automation; file name = run id. Keys: run, title, budget, params, steps. A step has an id and exactly one of agent, tool, shell, records.*, wait, or nested steps. Loops: `loop: {over, as, max}` or `{until, max}`. Gates: `gate: {approval: plan|proof|start|send, who: ...}`. Every outbound tool (send, post, pay) is preceded by a send gate. Triggers in app.json point at run ids; commands point at run ids.
{{end}}{{if .Wants "agent.md"}}- agent.md: front matter `name`, `model: {{.AgentModel}}`, `tools`, then plain instructions: what the agent does with this app's records, in this app's words. The agent works on content only and obeys rules 2 and 9. `tools` is a subset of what app.json capabilities allow, such as `[records.query, records.update]`.
{{end}}Every id used anywhere must exist: screens named in nav and `open`, runs named in triggers, commands and actions, record types named in refs, binds and capabilities. Every action must be covered by a capability. Do not write plan.json.

